This project pins `next@16.3.0`, a version ahead of your training data with
breaking API/convention changes from the Next.js you know. Before writing any
code, read the relevant guide under `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` (resolved
from the repo root — in monorepos the `next` package may not be visible from
elsewhere): `01-app/`, `02-pages/`, `03-architecture/`, `04-community/`. Heed
any deprecation notices found there.

`AGENTS.md` contains a banner block (`# This is NOT the Next.js you know`)
that is written/re-added by `next dev` on every run (see
`node_modules/next/dist/server/lib/generate-agent-files.js`). If it's absent
from a diff, that's expected — removing it only re-creates the uncommitted
change. Commit it as-is if it shows up staged; don't strip it.
